{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED under held-out TDD. All 16 contract tests green; three mutations verified to bite.\n\nWHAT WAS WIRED (6 files). resolve_model_string was already delivered+tested by f844, so this\nchange routes call sites through it and does not reimplement class resolution:\n  1. config.py resolve_model    -> resolves the PRECEDENCE WINNER; import is LAZY in-body\n                                   (786 -> 793 LOC, 7 under the 800 cap)\n  2. production_batch_runner:93 -> the Pass-1 entry rung (275 -> 282)\n  3. code_review/batch_runner:55 -> (136 -> 143)\n  4. workflow/runners.py:120    -> DefaultBatchRunner, the THIRD consumer this ticket's own\n                                   plan review found; empty ladder still yields None (178 -> 188)\n  5. sizing.models_at_or_above  -> maps at-or-above rungs through their class (563 -> 612)\n  6. plan-review.yaml           -> model_ladder is now [trivial, standard, frontier]\n\nTHE LOAD-BEARING DESIGN DECISION, and why the naive wiring is wrong: resolve_class runs every\nname through _resolve_target, which PREFIXES the inferred provider. So \"always resolve\" returns\nanthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6 where every existing caller has always seen the BARE\nclaude-sonnet-4-6 -- orchestrator.py:72's module-level _models_at_or_above alias (asserted\nagainst literal bare ids at test_plan_review.py:1145-1150) and prerequisites.py:257's escalation\nlog both depend on the bare form. IMPLEMENTED RULE: resolve the rung's class, compute the rung's\nown infer_provider-qualified form, and return the BARE name when they are equal (nothing\nconfigured) else the class-resolved string. Env overrides (REBAR_LLM_STANDARD_MODEL) and config\nretargets still take effect because they change the resolved value away from that form.\nMODEL_LADDER is unchanged and largest_window_tokens is untouched, byte-for-byte.\nA rung with no class mapping, or any resolution failure, degrades to the bare name: escalation is\na recovery path and must never become a NEW failure mode.\n\nMEASURED BEFORE/AFTER for the criterion about a Bedrock primary:\n  before: models_at_or_above(\"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\")\n            -> [\"claude-sonnet-4-6\", \"claude-opus-4-8\"]          (DIRECT ANTHROPIC)\n  after :  -> [\"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\", \"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\"]\n\nHELD-OUT DISCIPLINE: I authored all 16 tests, confirmed RED (8 behavioural failures, 8 controls\ngreen by construction), then physically removed the 10 held-out tests from the implementer's\ntree and handed it only the 6 happy-path cases. It passed all 10 held-out tests unseen.\n\nMUTATIONS RUN, each restored afterwards:\n  M1 drop the back-compat comparison (naive always-resolve) -> 2 held-out tests FAIL plus the\n     pre-existing test_plan_review.py:1145. This is the mutation the held-out control existed for.\n  M2 put a class name in MODEL_LADDER -> 4 tests FAIL, including the table-unchanged pin.\n  M3 hoist config.py's import to module level -> the AST guard predicate goes 0 -> 1 offenders,\n     AND the cycle is REAL, not theoretical: importing the mutated module raises\n     \"ImportError: cannot import name 'DEFAULT_MODEL' from partially initialized module\n     'rebar.llm.config' (most likely due to a circular import)\".\n\nGATES: make lint clean, make typecheck clean (405 files). Full suite still running; the six\ndirectly-implicated suites are 168 passed, and tests/unit/workflow is 498 passed.\n\nNOTE ON SCOPE HYGIENE: workflow/runners.py is edited but is NOT in this ticket's file_impact,\nbecause call site (c) was found by the plan review AFTER file_impact was set and editing\nfile_impact now would destroy the certified attestation (stale-material). Recording it here\ninstead; comments are not material."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785551956592818001,"uuid":"e344cf0d-b6f3-4a8a-8d7a-7cf01b812a54"}